It should never break a name
printWidth: 1
{% function res = block %}
{%- function res = "partial" -%}

It should break on named args
printWidth: 1
{% function res = "foo/bar", key1: val1, key2: (0..1) %}

It should not require commas (as per syntax) but add them when pretty printed
{% function res = "foo/bar" key1: val1 key2: (0..1) %}

It should not require spaces (as per syntax) but add them when pretty printed
{%function res = "foo/bar",key1:val1,key2:(0..1)%}

It should strip trailing commas by default
{% function res = "foo", %}
{% function res = "foo",product:product, %}

It should keep a bracket result target bracketed
{% function hash['key'] = "partial" %}
{% function hash["key"] = "partial" %}
{% function hash['a']['b'] = "partial" %}

It should normalise a dot result target to brackets
{% function obj.prop = "partial" %}
{% function obj.a.b = "partial" %}

It should format variable partial
{% function res = partial_name %}

It should preserve filters on function tag result (file-based)
{% function res = 'modules/core/api_calls/send', data: object, template: 'modules/openai/responses' | dig: 'results' %}

It should preserve filters on function tag with no args
{% function res = 'modules/core/api_calls/send' | dig: 'results' %}

It should break on long lines with filters
printWidth: 1
{% function res = 'modules/core/api_calls/send', data: object | dig: 'results' %}

It should preserve the append operator, which collects a partial result onto an array
{% assign items = [] %}
{% function items << "partials/fetch_item", id: 1 %}
{% function items << 'partials/fetch_item', id: 2 %}

It should preserve the append operator with a bracket target
{% function response["data"] << "partials/fetch_user", id: 1 %}
{% function response['a']['b'] << "partials/fetch_user" %}

It should normalise a dot target to brackets on append too
{% function obj.prop << "partial" %}

